All 15 tests pass. Here's what I fixed across the 3 source files:

**`src/auth.py`** — 2 bugs:
- `has_permission`: comparison was case-sensitive (`required in user_roles`). Fixed to compare lowercased.
- `is_admin_or_owner`: used `and` instead of `or`. Admin OR owner should grant access.

**`src/inventory.py`** — 4 bugs:
- `__init__`: mutable default `{}` was shared across instances. Changed to `None` default with `dict(initial) if initial else {}`.
- `add`: overwrote stock (`self._stock[sku] = qty`) instead of accumulating. Fixed to `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`.
- `reserve`: used `>=` to check availability, rejecting exact-quantity reservations. Changed to `>`.
- `release`: no guard against releasing more than reserved. Added a `ValueError` when `qty > current`.

**`src/text_utils.py`** — 3 bugs:
- `slugify`: didn't lowercase alphanumeric characters. Added `.lower()` call.
- `slugify`: `replace("--", "-")` only collapsed one pair of dashes. Replaced with a `while` loop.
- `truncate`: result length exceeded `max_len` because `text[:max_len] + suffix` added the suffix on top. Fixed to `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`.
